cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ftdoctor: checkpoint selection and failure diagnosis for fine-tuning runs"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: junglezke
repository-code: "https://github.com/junglezke/ftdoctor"
abstract: >-
  ftdoctor reads the training history a HuggingFace Trainer leaves in
  trainer_state.json -- locally or from a model repository on the Hub -- and
  reports whether the run overfit, which existing checkpoint to keep under a
  noise-aware criterion, and which documented failure modes the run shows.
  Thresholds were calibrated on 89 public fine-tuning logs.
keywords: [fine-tuning, large language models, overfitting, checkpoint selection, huggingface]
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
